course: religion-ethics
lesson: 12
title: The birth of Jesus
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The Gospels of Matthew and Luke tell how the angel Gabriel came to Mary, a young woman in Nazareth, and told her she would have a son, Jesus; Mary answered «Let it be to me according to your word».
explain: Joseph, the carpenter she was to marry, was told in a dream to take Mary as his wife and care for the child, and he quietly did so.
explain: A Roman census took them to Bethlehem; there was no room at the inn, so the baby was laid in a manger, an animal feeding trough, and angels sent shepherds to see him.
explain: Wise men from the East followed a star with gold, frankincense and myrrh, while jealous King Herod tried to kill the child, so the family fled to Egypt as refugees.
explain: Christians believe that in Jesus God himself became a human being (the Incarnation) — «Emmanuel, God with us» — and came humbly, close to poor and ordinary people; that is why Christmas is about welcome and giving, not only presents.
fact: The angel Gabriel told Mary in Nazareth that she would have a son, Jesus, the Son of God; this is called the Annunciation.
fact: Mary said yes to God: «Let it be to me according to your word».
fact: Joseph was a carpenter who was told in a dream to take Mary as his wife and care for the child.
fact: Mary and Joseph travelled to Bethlehem for a Roman census, a count of all the people, and there was no room for them at the inn.
fact: Jesus was laid in a manger, which is an animal feeding trough.
fact: Angels announced the birth to shepherds in the fields, singing «Glory to God, peace on earth», and the shepherds hurried to see the baby.
fact: Shepherds were ordinary, often looked-down-on workers, and Christians note that the good news came to them first.
fact: Wise men (magi) from the East followed a star and brought gold, frankincense and myrrh (two sweet-smelling tree gums); the Bible does not say there were three of them, only three gifts.
fact: King Herod was jealous and tried to kill the baby, so Jesus' family escaped to Egypt as refugees.
fact: Emmanuel is a name for Jesus meaning «God with us».
fact: The Incarnation is the Christian belief that God the Son became a real human being in Jesus.
fact: When Jesus was twelve he stayed behind in the Temple in Jerusalem asking and answering questions, and his parents searched for him for three days.
fact: After being found in the Temple, Jesus went home to Nazareth and obeyed his parents.
exercise: Who told Mary she would have a son? | The angel Gabriel | The prophet Elijah | King Herod | A wise man from the East
exercise: What is the Annunciation? | The angel's announcement to Mary that she would bear Jesus | The wise men's arrival at the house in Bethlehem | The family's flight into Egypt | The baptism of Jesus in the river Jordan
exercise: What did Mary answer the angel? | Let it be to me according to your word | I am far too young, so please choose someone else | Give me a sign from the stars first | I must ask Joseph before I answer
exercise: What was Joseph's trade? | A carpenter | A fisherman | A shepherd | A tax collector
exercise: How was Joseph told to take Mary as his wife? | In a dream | By a letter from the Temple | By a voice from a burning bush | By the wise men
exercise: Why did Mary and Joseph go to Bethlehem? | For a Roman census | To escape from King Herod | To visit the Temple for a feast | To find work as carpenters
exercise: What is a manger? | An animal feeding trough | A small wooden cradle for babies | A room at the back of an inn | A tent used by shepherds
exercise: Who were the first visitors the angels sent to the baby? | Shepherds from the fields | Priests from the Temple | Soldiers from the Roman army | The king and his servants
exercise: What gifts did the wise men bring? | Gold, frankincense and myrrh | Bread, wine and olive oil | Silver, a lamb and a blanket | Gold, a crown and a sceptre
exercise: How did the wise men find the way? | They followed a star | They followed the shepherds | They asked the innkeeper | They followed the river Jordan
exercise: Why did Jesus' family flee to Egypt? | King Herod wanted to kill the child | There was a famine in Bethlehem | Joseph found work there as a carpenter | The census sent them there
exercise: What does the name Emmanuel mean? | God with us | God is king | Prince of peace | Saviour of Israel
exercise: What is the Incarnation? | The belief that God the Son became a human being in Jesus | The feast when Christians give each other presents and eat dinner | The angel's visit to the shepherds at night | The star that led the wise men to Bethlehem
exercise: What did the boy Jesus do in the Temple at twelve? | He listened, asked and answered questions | He drove the money changers out of the Temple | He read the law aloud to the king and his court | He was crowned as the new king of the Jews
exercise: How long did Mary and Joseph search for the boy Jesus? | Three days | Forty days | One afternoon | Seven years
exercise: Why do Christians see meaning in Jesus being born in a stable? | God came humbly, close to poor and ordinary people | Stables were the most expensive rooms then | It shows Joseph did not want to pay | It shows Jesus was born a rich prince
test: lil bro: «3 kings came on camels cos the Bible says so». what does it actually say | Wise men came with three gifts; it never says three or kings | Exactly three kings came, named in the Bible | Twelve kings came with twelve gifts | Shepherds brought gold, frankincense and myrrh
test: Ella says Mary was told about the baby by a shepherd. Put her right. | It was the angel Gabriel | It was the innkeeper's wife | It was King Herod in a letter | It was John the Baptist's father
test: Muslim classmate: «We honour Jesus as a prophet too. What do Christians believe he is?» | God the Son who became human, God with us | Only a wise teacher like any other | An angel sent down from heaven in a human disguise | The son of King Herod
test: «why would God's son be born next to cows lol, makes no sense». Best answer for the olympiad? | Christians believe God chose to come humbly, close to ordinary people | It was a mistake because the inn lost the booking | It shows God did not care where he was born | Rich people always had babies in stables then
test: Why might the angels have gone to the shepherds first? | Good news came first to ordinary, looked-down-on workers | Shepherds were the richest and most important people nearby | Shepherds were the priests of Bethlehem | The king had ordered them to wait for it
test: New kid at school fled a war with her family. How does the Christmas story connect? | Jesus' family were refugees in Egypt too | Jesus' family stayed safely at home in Nazareth | The story says that refugees must always go back | The wise men were refugees running from Egypt
test: Joseph hardly says a word in the story. What does he show? | Quiet faithfulness: he protects Mary and the child | That he did not care about the baby | That he was too shy to speak to anyone | That he was angry and left them
test: dad lost me at the shops for an hour n went mental. is there a Bible story like that | The boy Jesus missing for three days, found in the Temple | The lost sheep found in the desert at night | The wise men losing the star for a week | Jonah lost inside the big fish
test: «Jesus asked loads of questions in the Temple so kids should never obey parents». Is that right? | No, he also went home and obeyed his parents | Yes, he never went back to Nazareth | Yes, the Bible says questions replace obeying | No, because he never asked any questions
test: Judge: «What does it mean to say God is Emmanuel?» | That in Jesus God came to live among people | That God lives only in the Temple | That God is far away, high above the stars, and never comes near | That God is a king like Herod
test: What did Herod feel about the newborn king? | Jealous fear for his own throne | Joy and a wish to give gifts | Nothing, he never heard of him | Pity and a wish to help the poor
exam: Identify the principal reason for which Joseph and Mary undertook the journey to Bethlehem. | A census decreed by the Roman authorities | Flight from the persecution of King Herod | Attendance at a festival in the Temple | Employment in the carpentry trade
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the doctrine of the Incarnation? | That God the Son assumed a truly human nature in Jesus | That Jesus was an angel in human appearance | That Jesus was solely an exemplary teacher | That God resides exclusively within the Temple at Jerusalem
exam: Ascertain, pursuant to the Gospel account, the gifts presented by the magi. | Gold, frankincense and myrrh | Bread, wine and oil | Silver, a lamb and linen | A crown, a sceptre and a robe
exam: It is given that the infant was placed in a manger. State the nature of the said object. | A trough from which animals feed | A cradle of carved wood | An upper room of an inn | A shepherd's portable tent
